# fbtv (Fubo → Emby & Jellyfin bridge) — context & memory

Before substantial work in this repository:

1. Read [CONTEXT.md](CONTEXT.md) for durable architecture and locked decisions
2. Read [WORKING_MEMORY.md](WORKING_MEMORY.md) for current focus, open questions, and next actions
3. Prefer [CREDITS.md](CREDITS.md) when touching Fubo client patterns borrowed from community bridges

While working:

- Update `WORKING_MEMORY.md` when focus, blockers, field notes, or next actions change
- Put lasting decisions in `CONTEXT.md` (and `CHANGELOG.md` / `docs/` when user-facing)
- Never write secrets, tokens, or raw `.env` values into context or memory files

This is a Python FastAPI sidecar for Emby and Jellyfin M3U + XMLTV (equal first-class targets) — not a native Emby or Jellyfin plugin. Short name / GitHub / Compose / GHCR image: **`fbtv`** (`https://github.com/cbodden/fbtv`, `ghcr.io/cbodden/fbtv`).
